cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use, reference, or build upon this research,
  please cite the research report using the preferred citation below.

title: "Apple Intelligence Research Report"

authors:
  - name: "Rainbow-SPY"

abstract: >-
  An empirical investigation of Apple Intelligence eligibility,
  regional restrictions, feature availability, and runtime behavior
  based on real-device testing and iOS sysdiagnose analysis.

  The research examines OSEligibility policies, MobileGestalt,
  countryd location estimates, Generative Experiences availability,
  ModelCatalog, ModelManager, Private Cloud Compute (PCC),
  and Apple Unified Logging.

  Particular attention is given to the relationship between
  device region, original sales identity, Apple Account country,
  geographic location, cellular networks, Wi-Fi, IP geolocation,
  and the execution of Apple Intelligence features.

  The study includes experimental findings from an iPhone 15 Pro Max,
  including Siri AI, image generation, Photos editing,
  and runtime regional restrictions affecting PCC requests.

